research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:1:{"id":"cex-exponential-not-uniformly-continuous-on-r","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"9fcc1e5af2a7a41cc0af29347e2e91274525499c0823280c5db2a8f0edfd0069","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"b57323d9a13b889de4db9a3a284d02c62c1db7e08c525e0f768a6d00dec9b242","verdict_item_sha256":"0e44e0f9ccc6fdcce7251bdfa97800ff9a422a11a3684ce8270dbc44ad5cc082","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"The rejection says continuity was not established, but the exact cited targets do establish it. thm-derivative-of-exponential states verbatim, 'The real exponential function is C^infinity' and 'In particular (exp)'=exp'; thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing states verbatim, 'The exponential function is continuous and strictly increasing on R.' Thus exp is continuous on each closed [x_n,y_n] and differentiable on its interior, exactly the hypotheses of cor-mean-value-theorem. No gap remains."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:2:{"id":"cor-exponential-is-a-bijection-onto-positive-reals","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"7a392fd7bc90e0c93cabf74d807929342f1e16c72563c8f672db92baf8c56a36","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"04d38d649f2aaa51e4b79784b9adf3563f554282598ba78e5bdd8af4159e22fa","verdict_item_sha256":"44a0ceb995d6727f62d8568b881f480b4c073bf6f159ee706fcdfc05553789b6","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"The rejection correctly identifies citation compression if cor-power-series-sums-are-continuous is read alone: it assumes an already-given power-series sum inside its radius. But the other exact L1 dependency, thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing, states verbatim, 'The exponential function is continuous and strictly increasing on R.' That immediately licenses the only continuity use. The redundant generic citation is imprecise but closes in under thirty seconds, so R1 forbids an edit."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:3:{"id":"ex-exponential-product-limit-at-negative-input","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"020c02ca1d20b49c114ca1d44ee2f45b18638ddf236d961e5374f9757b3b7306","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","item_sha256":"3bcd617417b2fca14e103c3632a20deab4ce64e463ff280cb5eeaa796bc2c55c","verdict_item_sha256":"1de2fea96c54b58d94af6891591babd5aa4689165ed04b2a9f7faf3d59b43b52","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"Confirmed fatal as a published sequence statement: def-canonical-natural says verbatim, 'iota(0)=0_F' and '1/iota(k) is undefined at k=0.' The displayed formula therefore does not define its claimed N-indexed sequence at n=0; the prose about a nonpositive base does not cure division by zero. The repair must define a_0 separately and use the product formula only for n>=1, with tail invariance cited exactly."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:4:{"id":"lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"edf7967518ed2d565358243833190996f4e0d8eea24c50e197c21903d1a74d45","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"15da00f5bddefff85d179f0f63ca4c41cd3e9c38e9032c0af41418d1d7fc18b7","verdict_item_sha256":"d9b8368b24337ca92e2dba8ae3882cf7bd8f5c03bca42a0633ca1c16ffd9260e","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"The Fact summary compresses two properties, but its exact cited lemma states verbatim that the canonical-natural map 'is strictly increasing' and '(mn) dot 1_F = (m dot 1_F)(n dot 1_F)'. Together with the cited factorial recurrence, these are precisely the two moves used in step 1.1. Expanding the Fact summary is a sub-thirty-second citation polish, hence confirmed nonfatal and not editable under R1."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:5:{"id":"lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"edf7967518ed2d565358243833190996f4e0d8eea24c50e197c21903d1a74d45","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"15da00f5bddefff85d179f0f63ca4c41cd3e9c38e9032c0af41418d1d7fc18b7","verdict_item_sha256":"d9b8368b24337ca92e2dba8ae3882cf7bd8f5c03bca42a0633ca1c16ffd9260e","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"DeepSeek identifies the same local Fact compression. lem-of-naturals-positive directly states strict increase and product preservation, and def-factorial-and-falling-factorial directly states the factorial recurrence. The cited targets close the ratio identity and inequality immediately; the mathematics is sound, the finding is nonfatal, and R1 forbids an edit."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:6:{"id":"thm-e-is-irrational","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"2a240f10616fb6de71483b6aaea7ff05b4e1247b5a7f2d29962af1434ef5053c","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","item_sha256":"733ef7c24688da2b73d1223df8b5729e86121937c6c4ee5e028d699cb63bb38a","verdict_item_sha256":"9bc53116e43987feabaf20728f5e9dcf24234497bca83566748433c83b15db05","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"Confirmed fatal. Step 3.1 is the load-bearing assertion that A is an integer, but L1 exports only factorial recurrence/nonzeroness and canonical-natural positivity. It does not license q|n!, k!|n!, the positive-integer-to-natural passage, or preservation through Z->Q->R. Without those facts the contradiction 0<A<1 cannot be applied to an embedded integer. The repair requires exact embedding and factorial-divisibility dependencies plus a typed local derivation."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:7:{"id":"thm-e-is-irrational","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"2a240f10616fb6de71483b6aaea7ff05b4e1247b5a7f2d29962af1434ef5053c","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","item_sha256":"733ef7c24688da2b73d1223df8b5729e86121937c6c4ee5e028d699cb63bb38a","verdict_item_sha256":"9bc53116e43987feabaf20728f5e9dcf24234497bca83566748433c83b15db05","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"Confirmed fatal for the same load-bearing typed gap. def-integers and def-rationals only construct quotient sets; they do not by themselves embed them into R. The exact lemmas lem-nat-embeds-int, lem-int-embeds-rat and lem-of-q-embeds are required, while thm-binomial-closed-formula plus factorial recurrence supplies the divisibility witnesses. Until those facts are stated and used, A's integrality is unproved."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:8:{"id":"thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"1631e9607c70db049a98f7ec0e6a0491dd6f8776a62ee1137954921fc3d8734b","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"9f325793011f0f447532084d85dffed78e3b3663bed6e6cc81e4df1464d055e2","verdict_item_sha256":"fc162f9dd3d013b423daa5062cb9cfce0151b493f05d7693dce2206c496994c5","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"L2 does not claim continuity alone suffices. It says the MVT applies to a continuous function and 'converts a positive interior derivative into strict increase'; L1 supplies that exp' exists everywhere and is positive. The cited cor-mean-value-theorem states exactly continuity on [a,b] plus differentiability on (a,b). Both hypotheses are present, so the alleged stronger-than-source statement is absent."}
research/audit/wave14-judge-adjudications.jsonl:9:{"id":"thm-exponential-limits-and-range","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","context_sha256":"7105668f32e4784576c769df1afbc933c57aefed40843a74413dd78958cde65a","outcome":"false_positive","item_sha256":"18663af32ce5049a512e2903201e40e5e5bf04f6945e2ef3792c59a3d819b444","verdict_item_sha256":"46abb129bd23221119f7afc3226d950eba1d49e02e4a40cefa99504c2eee745b","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-10T06:40:00.000Z","note":"The rejection overlooks the exact target's Combined forms paragraph. def-limits-at-infinity states verbatim: 'We write f(x) -> +infinity as x -> +infinity when for every real N there is a real M with f(x)>N for every x in A with x>M.' Step 1.1 proves exactly that quantified condition. The notion is defined and the use is licensed."}
