research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-thm-exponential-definition-equivalence.result.json:16:  "tail": "VERDICT: CLEAN\n\nBOUNDARY: Checked x=0 (series, product limit trivial, IVP y(0)=1, functional eqn gives F(0)=1 by continuity, Picard u_0=1). For x<0: product limit starts at n>|x| keeping base positive; Picard integral uses oriented integral; series and IVP global. Uniqueness of IVP and functional equation holds on all ℝ. No degenerate/empty constructions; every description yields a well‑defined function on ℝ.\n\nSOURCES: Inspected all six cited items: def-real-exponential-function-and-e, thm-derivative-of-exponential, thm-exponential-product-limit, thm-exponential-ivp-uniqueness, thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation, thm-picard-iterates-for-exponential. The quoted statements in the proof contract exactly match the required identifications; each correctly identifies its construction with the series‑defined exp. No mismatch in domains, hypotheses, or normalizations.\n\nCHECKED: Confirmed title, public Statement, numbered steps 1.1 and 2.1, and Remarks (none). Step 1.1 accurately cites the dependencies; step 2.1 correctly applies transitivity of equality. The proof is logically valid and non‑circular."
