research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:10877:## thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.log:10923:L2 -> thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation [Statement;1]: The exponential function is the unique continuous $F:\mathbb R\to(0,\infty)$ satisfying $F(x+y)=F(x)F(y)$ and $F(1)=e$. It is also the unique function differentiable at $0$ satisfying the functional equation, $F(0)=1$, and $F'(0)=1$.
