research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1058:### `thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation`
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1062:id: thm-normalized-exponential-functional-equation
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1064:title: "Regular normalized multiplicative Cauchy equations characterize the exponential"
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1097:**Given:** A function $F$ satisfying one of the two normalizations.
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1099:[L1] The exponential satisfies $\exp(x+y)=\exp(x)\exp(y)$, is continuous and positive, obeys $\exp(0)=1$, $\exp(1)=e$, and $\exp'=\exp$, and is the unique normalized solution of $y'=y$ ([[thm-exponential-addition-formula]], [[thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing]], [[cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity]], [[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]], [[thm-derivative-of-exponential]], [[thm-exponential-ivp-uniqueness]]).
research/audit/wave14-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-cex-discontinuous-multiplicative-cauchy-solution.prompt.md:1111:2.1 The exponential itself satisfies both normalizations, so both uniqueness assertions follow.  [step 1.1, step 1.2, L1, cases-exhaustive] ∎
